    <h1>Be VISIBLE when your buyers are asking AI</h1>

    <p>
      Your potential buyers have added ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude and Perplexity to how
      they research a purchase. When one of these engines is asked which vendors to
      shortlist, it confidently names a handful. If you're not among them, you're not
      even being considered, and you won't see the loss in your analytics.
    </p>

    <p>
      We find out where you stand. Fix what's keeping you out of the answer, and prove
      the fix worked.
    </p>

    <h2>VISIBILITY is not one problem, it's four</h2>

    <p>Before an engine recommends you, four separate things have to happen:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Retrieved:</strong> The AI engine needs to find your page. This fails
        when your site turns AI crawlers away, or if your pages get built in the
        visitor's browser and there is nothing for the engine to read.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cited:</strong> The engine needs to use your page as a source. This
        fails when there is nothing on the page that directly answers the question
        that's being asked.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Named:</strong> Your company needs to appear in the answer itself. In
        many cases, your page gets used as a source of information, while the answer
        goes on to recommend someone else.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Recommended:</strong> You want to be one of the vendors the engine
        actually puts forward. This rung is decided by reviews, analyst coverage and
        independent write-ups rather than by anything on your own site.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Fix it, prove it, maintain it</h2>

    <p>
      We restructure your content so engines can extract it, clean up the signals that
      identify you, open access to the crawlers that matter, and help you build the
      third-party presence that decides recommendation. Then we find out which of it
      worked, by holding a set of prompts and pages back untreated. If the treated set
      moves and the held-back set doesn't, the work caused it. You finish knowing which
      levers move your numbers, and you're able to pull them without us.
    </p>

    <p><a href="mailto:danny@visibility-audits.com">danny@visibility-audits.com</a></p>
  </body>
